## TESTING

### Guidelines for E2E

#### PLAYWRIGHT

- Initialize configuration only with Chromium/Desktop Chrome browser
- Use browser contexts for isolating test environments
- Implement the Page Object Model for maintainable tests
- Use locators for resilient element selection
- Leverage API testing for backend validation
- Implement visual comparison with expect(page).toHaveScreenshot()
- Use the codegen tool for test recording
- Leverage trace viewer for debugging test failures
- Implement test hooks for setup and teardown
- Use expect assertions with specific matchers
- Leverage parallel execution for faster test runs

#### ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION

- E2E tests use separate environment variables prefixed with `TEST_*`
- The `dev:e2e` script maps `TEST_SUPABASE_*` to `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_*` for client-side code
- Always use `npm run dev:e2e` (not `npm run dev`) when running E2E tests
- Run `npm run test:e2e:verify` to check environment configuration before testing
- Environment variables are baked into the client bundle at dev server start time
- Restart the dev server after changing environment variables

#### TEST STRUCTURE

- Use Page Object Model pattern (see `e2e/helpers/auth.helper.ts`)
- Store test data and selectors in `e2e/helpers/test-data.ts`
- Use descriptive test names that explain what is being tested
- Group related tests with `test.describe()`
- Use `test.beforeEach()` and `test.afterEach()` for setup/teardown
- Clear cookies and storage between tests to ensure clean state

